{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every static definition and responsive chart builder resolves to a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartSpec"},{"type":"text","value":".\nThe spec owns chart composition, scale factories or fixed scale instances, and\npresentation."}]},{"type":"code","value":"type ChartSpec<TMarks extends readonly ChartMark[]> = {\n  marks: TMarks\n  scales: ChartScales<TMarks>\n  guides?: boolean\n  color?: ChartColorOptions\n  gradients?: readonly ChartGradient[]\n  clip?: boolean\n  margin?: number | Partial<ChartMargin>\n  theme?: Partial<ChartTheme>\n}\n\ntype ChartScales<TMarks extends readonly ChartMark[]> = Readonly<\n  Record<string, ChartPositionScaleOptions | null>\n> & {\n  x: ChartPositionScaleOptions | null\n  y: ChartPositionScaleOptions | null\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"properties","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Properties"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Property"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Meaning"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"marks"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Yes"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ordered mark layers. Later scene nodes paint after earlier ones."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scales"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Yes"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cartesian scale registry. Reserved "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y"},{"type":"text","value":" entries are required; additional named scales are optional."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"guides"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":" to suppress both axes, grid lines, titles, and their implicit margins."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"color"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Shared categorical or quantitative color scale and optional legend."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gradients"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Linear and radial gradient resources consumed by SVG, Canvas, and React Native renderers."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"clip"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Clips the marks group to the resolved inner chart bounds in the default SVG and Canvas renderers."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"margin"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Locks all margins with a number or selected sides with a partial object. Omitted sides are measured automatically."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"theme"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Overrides default foreground, muted, grid, background, or palette tokens."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The detailed option contracts live in\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./scales-guides-and-color.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Scales, guides, and color"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Mark-specific\nchannels and defaults live in the "},{"type":"link","href":"./index.md#mark-reference","children":[{"type":"text","value":"mark reference"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"marks-and-layer-order","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Marks and layer order"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"marks"},{"type":"text","value":" is the grammar's composition unit:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { areaY, defineChart, lineY, ruleY } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { scaleUtc } from 'd3-scale'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\n\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  marks: [\n    areaY(rows, { x: 'date', y: 'value', fillOpacity: 0.12 }),\n    ruleY([target], {\n      stroke: '#dc2626',\n      strokeWidth: 1.5,\n      strokeDasharray: '4 2',\n    }),\n    lineY(rows, { x: 'date', y: 'value', points: true }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: { scale: scaleUtc },\n    y: { scale: scaleLinear, grid: true },\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each mark materializes channels for scale resolution, then emits renderer-\nneutral scene nodes and optional interaction points. Marks may use different\ndatum types in the same spec. Their inferred datum types become a union in\ninteraction callbacks."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A data-less "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"crosshair"},{"type":"text","value":" emits only transient focus-guide presentation. Place it\nbefore the first ordinary mark for an underlay or after ordinary marks for an\noverlay; it contributes no scale domain values or interaction points."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Built-in marks infer stable keys from a unique primitive top-level "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"},{"type":"text","value":", nested\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data.id"},{"type":"text","value":", or mark-owned positional candidate. Supply "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"key"},{"type":"text","value":" when none is\nunique. Mark IDs default from layer order; set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"},{"type":"text","value":" explicitly when a mark\nmust retain identity while its order changes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Built-in Cartesian, radial, and composite marks accept an optional\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderer"},{"type":"text","value":". Passing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"canvasChartRenderer"},{"type":"text","value":" opts that mark into Canvas while\nmarks without the option, including ordinary axes and guides, keep the host\nrenderer. The host groups adjacent runs without changing declaration order.\nSee "},{"type":"link","href":"./rendering-and-export.md#mark-level-renderers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mark-level renderers"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"required-positional-scales","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required positional scales"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scales.x"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scales.y"},{"type":"text","value":" are required. Supply a compatible factory for an\ninferred domain or a configured instance for a fixed domain:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const scales = {\n  x: { scale: scaleUtc },\n  y: { scale: scaleLinear },\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" for an unused dimension:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const horizontalThresholds = defineChart({\n  marks: [ruleY([25, 50, 75])],\n  scales: {\n    x: null,\n    y: { scale: scaleLinear().domain([0, 100]) },\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"axis: false"},{"type":"text","value":" hides an axis but does not remove its scale. A "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" entry says\nthat the scale does not exist. Scene compilation rejects a mark bound to a\nmissing scale."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Additional entries name independent mappings. Each named entry declares its\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"channel"},{"type":"text","value":", and marks opt into it with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"xScale"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"yScale"},{"type":"text","value":". See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./scales-guides-and-color.md#named-scales-and-multiple-axes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Named scales and multiple axes"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"guides-and-margins","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Guides and margins"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Guide visibility and geometry are separate:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scales.x.axis: false"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scales.y.axis: false"},{"type":"text","value":" hides one axis."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"guides: false"},{"type":"text","value":" hides all guides and removes their implicit margin."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grid"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"axis.line"},{"type":"text","value":" accept a boolean or a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartGuideLineStyle"},{"type":"text","value":" object\nwith stroke, opacity, width, dash, and line-cap overrides."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Omitted "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"margin"},{"type":"text","value":" sides are measured from ticks, rotation, titles, guide\nstrokes, edge overhang, color legends, and Cartesian "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"text"},{"type":"text","value":" marks."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"margin: 0"},{"type":"text","value":" locks every side to zero."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"margin: { left: 80 }"},{"type":"text","value":" locks only the left side."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Automatic margins contain guide and text-mark labels unless the side is locked\nor the plot is clipped; they do not choose a collision policy. Control dense\nguide labels with the scale's tick behavior, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ticks"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"format"},{"type":"text","value":", or\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tickRotate"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"clip-and-gradient-resources","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Clip and gradient resources"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"clip"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gradients"},{"type":"text","value":" are scene data consumed by the default SVG and Canvas\nrenderers:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const definition = defineChart({\n  marks,\n  scales: { x, y },\n  clip: true,\n  gradients: [\n    {\n      id: 'revenue',\n      y1: 1,\n      y2: 0,\n      stops: [\n        { offset: 0, color: '#2563eb', opacity: 0.08 },\n        { offset: 1, color: '#2563eb', opacity: 0.72 },\n      ],\n    },\n    {\n      type: 'radial',\n      id: 'highlight',\n      cx: 0.5,\n      cy: 0.5,\n      r: 0.5,\n      stops: [\n        { offset: 0, color: '#ffffff', opacity: 0.7 },\n        { offset: 1, color: '#2563eb', opacity: 0 },\n      ],\n    },\n  ],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reference a declared gradient from a mark paint as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"url(#revenue)"},{"type":"text","value":" or\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"url(#highlight)"},{"type":"text","value":". Coordinates and stop offsets use SVG-style\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"objectBoundingBox"},{"type":"text","value":" values normalized from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"idPrefix"},{"type":"text","value":" scopes\ngenerated SVG and React Native resource IDs when multiple charts share a\ndocument or native SVG tree. Stops keep their authored order. A stop before the\nprevious offset is clamped forward to that offset. See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./rendering-and-export.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rendering and export"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"theme","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Theme"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The complete default theme is exported as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultChartTheme"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"interface ChartTheme {\n  foreground: string\n  muted: string\n  grid: string\n  background: string\n  palette: readonly string[]\n  focusRing?: boolean | ChartFocusRingOptions\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"theme"},{"type":"text","value":" is partial. The palette is replaced as one value rather than merged by\nindex. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"focusRing"},{"type":"text","value":" supplies the default built-in focus ring presentation for\nevery chart using the theme. A definition-level "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"focusRing"},{"type":"text","value":" value overrides it.\nThe default palette uses CSS custom-property fallbacks:"}]},{"type":"code","value":".dashboard {\n  --ts-chart-1: #38bdf8;\n  --ts-chart-2: #fb7185;\n  --ts-chart-3: #4ade80;\n}","lang":"css"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Because the default foreground and guide colors use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"currentColor"},{"type":"text","value":", charts\ninherit light and dark mode without a JavaScript theme switch. Override theme\ntokens when the application needs an explicit visual system."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"properties","text":"Properties","level":2},{"id":"marks-and-layer-order","text":"Marks and layer order","level":2},{"id":"required-positional-scales","text":"Required positional scales","level":2},{"id":"guides-and-margins","text":"Guides and margins","level":2},{"id":"clip-and-gradient-resources","text":"Clip and gradient resources","level":2},{"id":"theme","text":"Theme","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nEvery static definition and responsive chart builder resolves to a `ChartSpec`.\nThe spec owns chart composition, scale factories or fixed scale instances, and\npresentation.\n\n```ts\ntype ChartSpec<TMarks extends readonly ChartMark[]> = {\n  marks: TMarks\n  scales: ChartScales<TMarks>\n  guides?: boolean\n  color?: ChartColorOptions\n  gradients?: readonly ChartGradient[]\n  clip?: boolean\n  margin?: number | Partial<ChartMargin>\n  theme?: Partial<ChartTheme>\n}\n\ntype ChartScales<TMarks extends readonly ChartMark[]> = Readonly<\n  Record<string, ChartPositionScaleOptions | null>\n> & {\n  x: ChartPositionScaleOptions | null\n  y: ChartPositionScaleOptions | null\n}\n```\n\n## Properties\n\n| Property    | Required | Meaning                                                                                                            |\n| ----------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `marks`     | Yes      | Ordered mark layers. Later scene nodes paint after earlier ones.                                                   |\n| `scales`    | Yes      | Cartesian scale registry. Reserved `x` and `y` entries are required; additional named scales are optional.         |\n| `guides`    | No       | Set to `false` to suppress both axes, grid lines, titles, and their implicit margins.                              |\n| `color`     | No       | Shared categorical or quantitative color scale and optional legend.                                                |\n| `gradients` | No       | Linear and radial gradient resources consumed by SVG, Canvas, and React Native renderers.                          |\n| `clip`      | No       | Clips the marks group to the resolved inner chart bounds in the default SVG and Canvas renderers.                  |\n| `margin`    | No       | Locks all margins with a number or selected sides with a partial object. Omitted sides are measured automatically. |\n| `theme`     | No       | Overrides default foreground, muted, grid, background, or palette tokens.                                          |\n\nThe detailed option contracts live in\n[Scales, guides, and color](./scales-guides-and-color.md). Mark-specific\nchannels and defaults live in the [mark reference](./index.md#mark-reference).\n\n## Marks and layer order\n\n`marks` is the grammar's composition unit:\n\n```ts\nimport { areaY, defineChart, lineY, ruleY } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { scaleUtc } from 'd3-scale'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\n\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  marks: [\n    areaY(rows, { x: 'date', y: 'value', fillOpacity: 0.12 }),\n    ruleY([target], {\n      stroke: '#dc2626',\n      strokeWidth: 1.5,\n      strokeDasharray: '4 2',\n    }),\n    lineY(rows, { x: 'date', y: 'value', points: true }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: { scale: scaleUtc },\n    y: { scale: scaleLinear, grid: true },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nEach mark materializes channels for scale resolution, then emits renderer-\nneutral scene nodes and optional interaction points. Marks may use different\ndatum types in the same spec. Their inferred datum types become a union in\ninteraction callbacks.\n\nA data-less `crosshair` emits only transient focus-guide presentation. Place it\nbefore the first ordinary mark for an underlay or after ordinary marks for an\noverlay; it contributes no scale domain values or interaction points.\n\nBuilt-in marks infer stable keys from a unique primitive top-level `id`, nested\n`data.id`, or mark-owned positional candidate. Supply `key` when none is\nunique. Mark IDs default from layer order; set `id` explicitly when a mark\nmust retain identity while its order changes.\n\nBuilt-in Cartesian, radial, and composite marks accept an optional\n`renderer`. Passing `canvasChartRenderer` opts that mark into Canvas while\nmarks without the option, including ordinary axes and guides, keep the host\nrenderer. The host groups adjacent runs without changing declaration order.\nSee [Mark-level renderers](./rendering-and-export.md#mark-level-renderers).\n\n## Required positional scales\n\n`scales.x` and `scales.y` are required. Supply a compatible factory for an\ninferred domain or a configured instance for a fixed domain:\n\n```ts\nconst scales = {\n  x: { scale: scaleUtc },\n  y: { scale: scaleLinear },\n}\n```\n\nUse `null` for an unused dimension:\n\n```ts\nconst horizontalThresholds = defineChart({\n  marks: [ruleY([25, 50, 75])],\n  scales: {\n    x: null,\n    y: { scale: scaleLinear().domain([0, 100]) },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n`axis: false` hides an axis but does not remove its scale. A `null` entry says\nthat the scale does not exist. Scene compilation rejects a mark bound to a\nmissing scale.\n\nAdditional entries name independent mappings. Each named entry declares its\n`channel`, and marks opt into it with `xScale` or `yScale`. See\n[Named scales and multiple axes](./scales-guides-and-color.md#named-scales-and-multiple-axes).\n\n## Guides and margins\n\nGuide visibility and geometry are separate:\n\n- `scales.x.axis: false` or `scales.y.axis: false` hides one axis.\n- `guides: false` hides all guides and removes their implicit margin.\n- `grid` and `axis.line` accept a boolean or a `ChartGuideLineStyle` object\n  with stroke, opacity, width, dash, and line-cap overrides.\n- Omitted `margin` sides are measured from ticks, rotation, titles, guide\n  strokes, edge overhang, color legends, and Cartesian `text` marks.\n- `margin: 0` locks every side to zero.\n- `margin: { left: 80 }` locks only the left side.\n\nAutomatic margins contain guide and text-mark labels unless the side is locked\nor the plot is clipped; they do not choose a collision policy. Control dense\nguide labels with the scale's tick behavior, `ticks`, `format`, or\n`tickRotate`.\n\n## Clip and gradient resources\n\n`clip` and `gradients` are scene data consumed by the default SVG and Canvas\nrenderers:\n\n```ts\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  marks,\n  scales: { x, y },\n  clip: true,\n  gradients: [\n    {\n      id: 'revenue',\n      y1: 1,\n      y2: 0,\n      stops: [\n        { offset: 0, color: '#2563eb', opacity: 0.08 },\n        { offset: 1, color: '#2563eb', opacity: 0.72 },\n      ],\n    },\n    {\n      type: 'radial',\n      id: 'highlight',\n      cx: 0.5,\n      cy: 0.5,\n      r: 0.5,\n      stops: [\n        { offset: 0, color: '#ffffff', opacity: 0.7 },\n        { offset: 1, color: '#2563eb', opacity: 0 },\n      ],\n    },\n  ],\n})\n```\n\nReference a declared gradient from a mark paint as `url(#revenue)` or\n`url(#highlight)`. Coordinates and stop offsets use SVG-style\n`objectBoundingBox` values normalized from `0` to `1`. `idPrefix` scopes\ngenerated SVG and React Native resource IDs when multiple charts share a\ndocument or native SVG tree. Stops keep their authored order. A stop before the\nprevious offset is clamped forward to that offset. See\n[Rendering and export](./rendering-and-export.md).\n\n## Theme\n\nThe complete default theme is exported as `defaultChartTheme`:\n\n```ts\ninterface ChartTheme {\n  foreground: string\n  muted: string\n  grid: string\n  background: string\n  palette: readonly string[]\n  focusRing?: boolean | ChartFocusRingOptions\n}\n```\n\n`theme` is partial. The palette is replaced as one value rather than merged by\nindex. `focusRing` supplies the default built-in focus ring presentation for\nevery chart using the theme. A definition-level `focusRing` value overrides it.\nThe default palette uses CSS custom-property fallbacks:\n\n```css\n.dashboard {\n  --ts-chart-1: #38bdf8;\n  --ts-chart-2: #fb7185;\n  --ts-chart-3: #4ade80;\n}\n```\n\nBecause the default foreground and guide colors use `currentColor`, charts\ninherit light and dark mode without a JavaScript theme switch. Override theme\ntokens when the application needs an explicit visual system.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Chart Spec\ndescription: Reference for marks, axes, color, gradients, clipping, margins, guides, and themes in a TanStack Charts spec.\n---\n\nEvery static definition and responsive chart builder resolves to a `ChartSpec`.\nThe spec owns chart composition, scale factories or fixed scale instances, and\npresentation.\n\n```ts\ntype ChartSpec<TMarks extends readonly ChartMark[]> = {\n  marks: TMarks\n  scales: ChartScales<TMarks>\n  guides?: boolean\n  color?: ChartColorOptions\n  gradients?: readonly ChartGradient[]\n  clip?: boolean\n  margin?: number | Partial<ChartMargin>\n  theme?: Partial<ChartTheme>\n}\n\ntype ChartScales<TMarks extends readonly ChartMark[]> = Readonly<\n  Record<string, ChartPositionScaleOptions | null>\n> & {\n  x: ChartPositionScaleOptions | null\n  y: ChartPositionScaleOptions | null\n}\n```\n\n## Properties\n\n| Property    | Required | Meaning                                                                                                            |\n| ----------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `marks`     | Yes      | Ordered mark layers. Later scene nodes paint after earlier ones.                                                   |\n| `scales`    | Yes      | Cartesian scale registry. Reserved `x` and `y` entries are required; additional named scales are optional.         |\n| `guides`    | No       | Set to `false` to suppress both axes, grid lines, titles, and their implicit margins.                              |\n| `color`     | No       | Shared categorical or quantitative color scale and optional legend.                                                |\n| `gradients` | No       | Linear and radial gradient resources consumed by SVG, Canvas, and React Native renderers.                          |\n| `clip`      | No       | Clips the marks group to the resolved inner chart bounds in the default SVG and Canvas renderers.                  |\n| `margin`    | No       | Locks all margins with a number or selected sides with a partial object. Omitted sides are measured automatically. |\n| `theme`     | No       | Overrides default foreground, muted, grid, background, or palette tokens.                                          |\n\nThe detailed option contracts live in\n[Scales, guides, and color](./scales-guides-and-color.md). Mark-specific\nchannels and defaults live in the [mark reference](./index.md#mark-reference).\n\n## Marks and layer order\n\n`marks` is the grammar's composition unit:\n\n```ts\nimport { areaY, defineChart, lineY, ruleY } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { scaleUtc } from 'd3-scale'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\n\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  marks: [\n    areaY(rows, { x: 'date', y: 'value', fillOpacity: 0.12 }),\n    ruleY([target], {\n      stroke: '#dc2626',\n      strokeWidth: 1.5,\n      strokeDasharray: '4 2',\n    }),\n    lineY(rows, { x: 'date', y: 'value', points: true }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: { scale: scaleUtc },\n    y: { scale: scaleLinear, grid: true },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nEach mark materializes channels for scale resolution, then emits renderer-\nneutral scene nodes and optional interaction points. Marks may use different\ndatum types in the same spec. Their inferred datum types become a union in\ninteraction callbacks.\n\nA data-less `crosshair` emits only transient focus-guide presentation. Place it\nbefore the first ordinary mark for an underlay or after ordinary marks for an\noverlay; it contributes no scale domain values or interaction points.\n\nBuilt-in marks infer stable keys from a unique primitive top-level `id`, nested\n`data.id`, or mark-owned positional candidate. Supply `key` when none is\nunique. Mark IDs default from layer order; set `id` explicitly when a mark\nmust retain identity while its order changes.\n\nBuilt-in Cartesian, radial, and composite marks accept an optional\n`renderer`. Passing `canvasChartRenderer` opts that mark into Canvas while\nmarks without the option, including ordinary axes and guides, keep the host\nrenderer. The host groups adjacent runs without changing declaration order.\nSee [Mark-level renderers](./rendering-and-export.md#mark-level-renderers).\n\n## Required positional scales\n\n`scales.x` and `scales.y` are required. Supply a compatible factory for an\ninferred domain or a configured instance for a fixed domain:\n\n```ts\nconst scales = {\n  x: { scale: scaleUtc },\n  y: { scale: scaleLinear },\n}\n```\n\nUse `null` for an unused dimension:\n\n```ts\nconst horizontalThresholds = defineChart({\n  marks: [ruleY([25, 50, 75])],\n  scales: {\n    x: null,\n    y: { scale: scaleLinear().domain([0, 100]) },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n`axis: false` hides an axis but does not remove its scale. A `null` entry says\nthat the scale does not exist. Scene compilation rejects a mark bound to a\nmissing scale.\n\nAdditional entries name independent mappings. Each named entry declares its\n`channel`, and marks opt into it with `xScale` or `yScale`. See\n[Named scales and multiple axes](./scales-guides-and-color.md#named-scales-and-multiple-axes).\n\n## Guides and margins\n\nGuide visibility and geometry are separate:\n\n- `scales.x.axis: false` or `scales.y.axis: false` hides one axis.\n- `guides: false` hides all guides and removes their implicit margin.\n- `grid` and `axis.line` accept a boolean or a `ChartGuideLineStyle` object\n  with stroke, opacity, width, dash, and line-cap overrides.\n- Omitted `margin` sides are measured from ticks, rotation, titles, guide\n  strokes, edge overhang, color legends, and Cartesian `text` marks.\n- `margin: 0` locks every side to zero.\n- `margin: { left: 80 }` locks only the left side.\n\nAutomatic margins contain guide and text-mark labels unless the side is locked\nor the plot is clipped; they do not choose a collision policy. Control dense\nguide labels with the scale's tick behavior, `ticks`, `format`, or\n`tickRotate`.\n\n## Clip and gradient resources\n\n`clip` and `gradients` are scene data consumed by the default SVG and Canvas\nrenderers:\n\n```ts\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  marks,\n  scales: { x, y },\n  clip: true,\n  gradients: [\n    {\n      id: 'revenue',\n      y1: 1,\n      y2: 0,\n      stops: [\n        { offset: 0, color: '#2563eb', opacity: 0.08 },\n        { offset: 1, color: '#2563eb', opacity: 0.72 },\n      ],\n    },\n    {\n      type: 'radial',\n      id: 'highlight',\n      cx: 0.5,\n      cy: 0.5,\n      r: 0.5,\n      stops: [\n        { offset: 0, color: '#ffffff', opacity: 0.7 },\n        { offset: 1, color: '#2563eb', opacity: 0 },\n      ],\n    },\n  ],\n})\n```\n\nReference a declared gradient from a mark paint as `url(#revenue)` or\n`url(#highlight)`. Coordinates and stop offsets use SVG-style\n`objectBoundingBox` values normalized from `0` to `1`. `idPrefix` scopes\ngenerated SVG and React Native resource IDs when multiple charts share a\ndocument or native SVG tree. Stops keep their authored order. A stop before the\nprevious offset is clamped forward to that offset. See\n[Rendering and export](./rendering-and-export.md).\n\n## Theme\n\nThe complete default theme is exported as `defaultChartTheme`:\n\n```ts\ninterface ChartTheme {\n  foreground: string\n  muted: string\n  grid: string\n  background: string\n  palette: readonly string[]\n  focusRing?: boolean | ChartFocusRingOptions\n}\n```\n\n`theme` is partial. The palette is replaced as one value rather than merged by\nindex. `focusRing` supplies the default built-in focus ring presentation for\nevery chart using the theme. A definition-level `focusRing` value overrides it.\nThe default palette uses CSS custom-property fallbacks:\n\n```css\n.dashboard {\n  --ts-chart-1: #38bdf8;\n  --ts-chart-2: #fb7185;\n  --ts-chart-3: #4ade80;\n}\n```\n\nBecause the default foreground and guide colors use `currentColor`, charts\ninherit light and dark mode without a JavaScript theme switch. Override theme\ntokens when the application needs an explicit visual system.\n"}
